      award_pot: 'This game has no pot to award.',
      play_card: 'Tile must match an open end of the layout (same pip value). For spinners, placement order applies: both sides must be filled before the exposed end.',
      draw: 'Legal only when you have no tile that matches any open end of the layout.',
      discard: 'This game has no discard pile.',
      pass: 'This game has no pass action.',
      bid: 'This game has no bid action.',
      meld: 'This game has no meld action.',
      go_out: 'This game has no go-out action.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first player or partnership to reach 61 points. Score during play by making the open ends of the layout total a multiple of five; at end of each hand, subtract penalty points for pips left in hand (rounded to nearest multiple of five, divided by five).',
      'Turn-flow example: Domino game in the Fives family. All doubles are spinners. Score when layout pip total is a multiple of 5. Play to 61 points.',
      "Scoring example: After each tile is set, sum the pips on all open ends of the layout; if the total is a multiple of 5 (5, 10, 15, 20...), the player scores that total divided by 5. An exposed double counts both its pips until tiles have been played on both sides of it. At end of hand, each player's remaining pips are rounded to the nearest multiple of 5, divided by 5, and subtracted from their score. First to 61 points wins. First player or partnership to reach 61 points wins. Tie: play further hands until one leads..",
